    "policy": {
      "body": "Select four or five dated, source-ordered text blocks, sometimes across adjacent digest items; normalize visible whitespace, remove non-prose blocks. Only Treasury includes the named public-official salutation/signature. Agency newsletter title used as signature in two constructed controls.",
      "exposure": "Screen normalized exact 12-token fragments in all prepared ordinary controls against known project input history and across the six sources. Does not establish model-pretraining independence.",
      "human": "Per source, create exact original excerpt, a same-issue whole donor paragraph, a same-issue single sentence donor edit, unchanged excerpt plus an agency paragraph sentence as a plaintext quote, and unchanged excerpt plus the actual publisher template or signature text. These are reproducible source-only splices, not collected naturally edited emails.",
      "paired_mixed": "Use the same exact AI body edit twice per generator, once plain and once with both the same quote and publisher template. Archive records refer only to source prose. MIME headers, packaging and alternative/attachment are synthetic.",
      "rights": "Federal government work, 17 U.S.C. §§ 101 and 105. Only issue-body prose and publisher-authored title, editorial boilerplate or correspondence signature. An archive renderer hosts the pages; its templates and assets are excluded.",
      "source": "Archived 2021 bulletins delivered by six different U.S. government publishers. Manually verify agency byline, date, direct federal employee/agency prose and content geometry without classifier scores. One issue per publisher. Exclude third-party quoted material, images, navigation, vendor boilerplate, headers and contacts."
    },
